WEBVTT

00:00:01.390 --> 00:00:04.980
Satoshi, who aims to battle
the Supreme Monarch, Dande...

00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:10.110
And Go, who dreams of catching every Pokémon
to work his way up to Mew...

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:15.340
This is the story of their lives and adventures.

00:00:19.310 --> 00:00:30.440
One, two! One, two!

00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:31.800
Hey!

00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:38.550
What’s up, Satoshi?
Why’d you suddenly start jogging?

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:41.540
Because my ranking dropped
after that last battle.

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:43.230
I’d better win the next one!

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:45.660
You want revenge, too,
right, Riolu?

00:00:46.790 --> 00:00:49.690
So I thought we’d better
train hard.

00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:54.130
I see. Well then,
I’ll help you!

00:00:54.130 --> 00:00:55.450
Thanks!

00:00:55.450 --> 00:00:58.740
One, two! One, two!

00:00:58.740 --> 00:01:01.230
This is an official
battle announcement.

00:01:01.230 --> 00:01:03.000
All right! This is it!

00:01:07.870 --> 00:01:12.210
This battle will be a 1v1.

00:01:12.210 --> 00:01:15.470
All right, both sides send out
your Pokémon at the same time.

00:01:15.890 --> 00:01:16.470
3!

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:17.470
2!

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:18.470
1!

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:19.720
Go!

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:22.810
Riolu, I choose you!

00:01:22.810 --> 00:01:24.560
Go, Octan!

00:01:27.310 --> 00:01:29.370
You got this, Satoshi!

00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:35.110
Octan, huh?
It’s a bit like Otosupus.

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:43.240
Suits me just fine!
Riolu, stay back as much as you can!

00:01:45.710 --> 00:01:47.460
Battle, start!

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:49.340
Hit it with a flurry of
Vacuum Waves!

00:01:54.160 --> 00:01:55.590
Octan! Psyche-Beam!

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:04.810
Octan! Wrap!

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:10.020
Run, Riolu!

00:02:11.270 --> 00:02:12.360
Octan Cannon!

00:02:21.570 --> 00:02:24.910
Riolu is unable to battle!
Octan wins!

00:02:25.850 --> 00:02:26.890
Riolu!

00:02:33.850 --> 00:02:35.940
This is an official
battle announcement.

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:39.720
I <i>swear</i> I’ll make up
for my losses!

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:16.980
Climb Your Way Out of Sand Hell!
Satoshi and Go,

00:04:17.460 --> 00:04:20.820
All right, both sides send out
your Pokémon at the same time.

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:21.780
3!

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:22.740
2!

00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:23.700
1!

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:25.200
Go!

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:27.370
Go, Riolu!

00:04:27.770 --> 00:04:30.030
You can do it, Dokukurage!

00:04:34.230 --> 00:04:38.130
Dokukurage... Another one
that’ll be hard to fight up close.

00:04:38.130 --> 00:04:40.720
Riolu, no getting close!

00:04:41.630 --> 00:04:43.390
Hang in there!

00:04:44.970 --> 00:04:47.430
Battle, start!

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:48.680
Bubble Beam!

00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:50.610
Dodge and fire
a Vacuum Wave flurry!

00:04:56.730 --> 00:04:58.190
No, get back!

00:05:00.730 --> 00:05:03.030
Dokukurage,
use your Bind attack!

00:05:05.030 --> 00:05:05.780
Riolu!

00:05:05.780 --> 00:05:06.780
Poison Needle!

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:20.720
Riolu is unable to battle!
Dokukurage wins!

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:22.170
Riolu!

00:05:22.170 --> 00:05:24.220
Based on the results of this battle,

00:05:24.220 --> 00:05:28.390
the Pokémon World Championships
rankings will be updated!

00:05:34.930 --> 00:05:39.020
I-I’ve dropped from the Super Class
back to the Normal Class...

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:40.700
Oh, no...

00:05:42.640 --> 00:05:43.980
Satoshi...

00:05:45.820 --> 00:05:46.360
Kinsetsu City, Hoenn Region

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:50.140
Meanwhile, in Kinsetsu City
in Hoenn,
Kinsetsu City, Hoenn Region

00:05:50.140 --> 00:05:52.580
a bizarre event was
taking place.
Kinsetsu City, Hoenn Region

00:05:53.800 --> 00:05:56.580
What is going on here?

00:05:56.580 --> 00:05:59.960
I don’t know. It’s been like this
since the morning.

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:02.490
What’s going on in there?

00:06:02.490 --> 00:06:04.800
How would we know?

00:06:13.220 --> 00:06:14.580
A song?

00:06:14.580 --> 00:06:16.100
It’s beautiful.

00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:19.750
What... is even happening?

00:06:19.750 --> 00:06:21.700
Who knows...?

00:06:21.700 --> 00:06:22.950
Yeah...

00:06:37.280 --> 00:06:40.460
A singing voice heard
from inside a sandstorm, huh?

00:06:40.460 --> 00:06:45.250
People are going into the sandstorm,
lured by the voice...

00:06:45.250 --> 00:06:47.170
That’s rather concerning.

00:06:47.170 --> 00:06:49.990
Could it be the work of
an unknown Pokémon?

00:06:49.990 --> 00:06:50.630
What?!

00:06:50.630 --> 00:06:51.800
Unknown Pokémon?!

00:06:52.170 --> 00:06:54.970
If it is, then I gotta catch it!

00:06:54.970 --> 00:07:00.940
Director Sakuragi! Please let us go
investigate the sandstorm as your research fellows!

00:07:00.940 --> 00:07:04.270
All right. But don’t be too reckless.

00:07:04.270 --> 00:07:05.380
Of course.

00:07:05.380 --> 00:07:07.900
All right... Come on, Satoshi!

00:07:09.420 --> 00:07:12.950
I dropped a class...
Dropped a class...

00:07:12.950 --> 00:07:15.100
Hey, now! Cheer up!

00:07:15.100 --> 00:07:17.690
Come on, you’ve lost
a few times, but so what?

00:07:17.690 --> 00:07:23.410
Yeah, I lost.
Three times in a row, at that!

00:07:25.080 --> 00:07:28.920
At this rate, challenging Mr. Dande
will be a dream within another dream...

00:07:28.920 --> 00:07:30.930
What are you saying, Satoshi?

00:07:30.930 --> 00:07:34.800
I just <i>know</i> meeting a rare Pokémon
will get you all fired up!

00:07:34.800 --> 00:07:36.800
Cheer up, Satoshi.

00:07:36.800 --> 00:07:40.150
I expect good news regarding
this unknown Pokémon, Go.

00:07:47.090 --> 00:07:50.320
Whoa, the city’s totally buried in sand.

00:07:50.320 --> 00:07:54.420
If this really is a Pokémon’s handiwork,
then that’s amazing, yeah?

00:07:55.990 --> 00:07:58.200
Get it together, Satoshi!

00:07:58.200 --> 00:07:59.950
We’re just about
to go investigating!

00:08:01.430 --> 00:08:03.480
Right... Sorry...

00:08:07.740 --> 00:08:09.200
This is it, huh?

00:08:15.140 --> 00:08:18.270
It kinda feels like
it’s calling for us.

00:08:18.270 --> 00:08:22.010
I can kinda understand
why some people went inside.

00:08:22.010 --> 00:08:23.440
Let’s go check it out!

00:08:23.440 --> 00:08:26.650
Oh! <i>There’s</i> the Satoshi I know!

00:08:26.650 --> 00:08:30.330
All right...
Go-Go Goggles, go!

00:08:30.330 --> 00:08:30.990
Grin!

00:08:38.040 --> 00:08:39.670
Messon?

00:08:43.320 --> 00:08:45.630
All right! Into the storm!

00:08:45.630 --> 00:08:47.170
Let’s go!

00:09:12.380 --> 00:09:14.330
The storm subsided?

00:09:16.350 --> 00:09:17.410
Whoa!

00:09:17.410 --> 00:09:19.420
It’s a literal desert!

00:09:23.900 --> 00:09:25.580
Somebody!

00:09:25.580 --> 00:09:27.190
Help!

00:09:27.190 --> 00:09:28.050
Let’s have a look!

00:09:28.050 --> 00:09:28.940
Yeah!

00:09:35.180 --> 00:09:36.720
Help!

00:09:37.580 --> 00:09:38.670
What’s this?

00:09:38.670 --> 00:09:39.890
What’s going on?

00:09:39.890 --> 00:09:43.220
I can’t get out! Please help!

00:09:47.980 --> 00:09:49.190
No way!

00:09:50.260 --> 00:09:51.280
W-What’s that?

00:09:51.950 --> 00:09:55.720
Nuckrar! Ant Pit Pokémon!
Ground type!

00:09:55.720 --> 00:09:57.900
Its nest is a sloped,
bowl-like pit dug in sand!

00:09:57.900 --> 00:10:00.910
It patiently waits for prey
to tumble down the pit!

00:10:00.910 --> 00:10:03.500
Its giant jaws have enough strength
to crush even boulders!

00:10:04.040 --> 00:10:06.380
So it was a Nuckrar’s nest?

00:10:07.310 --> 00:10:09.750
The only way to save them
is to catch it!

00:10:14.050 --> 00:10:18.720
One more try!
This time, with a super curveball!

00:10:32.160 --> 00:10:35.720
Nuckrar’s data will be
added to the Index!

00:10:37.050 --> 00:10:39.810
Oh, thank you!
You really saved us!

00:10:39.810 --> 00:10:42.280
We were just suddenly
sucked into that hole!

00:10:42.280 --> 00:10:45.800
I didn’t know what to do.
Really, thank you!

00:10:52.280 --> 00:10:54.090
I hear it again.

00:10:55.400 --> 00:10:56.960
Seems it’s coming
from over there.

00:11:17.800 --> 00:11:18.400
What’s that?

00:11:20.970 --> 00:11:22.460
Vibrava?

00:11:23.760 --> 00:11:27.950
Vibrava! Vibration Pokémon!
Ground/Dragon type!

00:11:27.950 --> 00:11:32.230
It generates supersonic waves by
vigorously making its two wings vibrate!

00:11:32.230 --> 00:11:35.160
These are so powerful,
they can bring on headaches in people!

00:11:35.160 --> 00:11:38.480
All right! Another chance for a catch!

00:11:41.560 --> 00:11:43.390
Is this what it meant?!

00:11:45.020 --> 00:11:47.850
Curveball, go!

00:11:47.850 --> 00:11:49.090
Rabbifoot!

00:12:02.480 --> 00:12:06.200
Vibrava’s data will be
added to the Index!

00:12:06.200 --> 00:12:08.410
You did it, Go!

00:12:09.610 --> 00:12:10.950
Hang on.

00:12:10.950 --> 00:12:15.940
Nuckrar evolves into Vibrava,
which then evolves into...

00:12:17.710 --> 00:12:19.340
Could it be...?

00:12:27.220 --> 00:12:28.630
Flygon!

00:12:32.350 --> 00:12:34.250
Pocket Monsters!

00:12:38.570 --> 00:12:43.490
Nuckrar

00:12:44.890 --> 00:12:49.140
Flygon! Spirit Pokémon!
Ground/Dragon type!

00:12:49.140 --> 00:12:51.040
Known as “The Desert Spirit,”

00:12:51.040 --> 00:12:55.660
this Pokémon hides in the sandstorms
it causes by beating its wings!

00:12:56.190 --> 00:13:00.130
Satoshi, that singing
came from Flygon.

00:13:00.130 --> 00:13:05.400
The singing voice was the sound caused
by the sand rubbing up against Flygon’s wings.

00:13:05.400 --> 00:13:09.150
It probably caused the sandstorms
to make it so people couldn’t get in,

00:13:09.150 --> 00:13:11.640
so it could build its nest here.

00:13:11.640 --> 00:13:15.430
I see. But this isn’t good, is it?

00:13:15.430 --> 00:13:17.860
No. We have to
stop the sandstorm!

00:13:19.020 --> 00:13:19.860
Go!

00:13:22.780 --> 00:13:26.440
I guess it won’t let me catch it easily.

00:13:26.440 --> 00:13:28.810
Satoshi, help me battle it!

00:13:30.580 --> 00:13:31.410
Okay...

00:13:32.410 --> 00:13:34.880
Messon, go!

00:13:39.300 --> 00:13:40.630
Come on, Pikachu!

00:13:42.380 --> 00:13:43.680
100,000 Volts!

00:13:53.340 --> 00:13:56.020
Satoshi! Flygon is a Ground type!

00:13:56.020 --> 00:13:57.990
Electric moves won’t affect it!

00:13:59.060 --> 00:14:00.740
Oh, of course!

00:14:00.740 --> 00:14:02.810
What am I doing?

00:14:02.810 --> 00:14:04.150
Pikachu, get back!

00:14:06.120 --> 00:14:07.490
Go, Riolu!

00:14:08.320 --> 00:14:10.180
Use a Vacuum Wave flurry!

00:14:20.320 --> 00:14:22.450
It’s hopeless!
They don’t work at all!

00:14:22.450 --> 00:14:25.420
We have to do something
about that sandstorm!

00:14:25.420 --> 00:14:27.610
Messon! Water Gun!

00:14:34.650 --> 00:14:36.990
Not yet... Keep going!

00:14:36.990 --> 00:14:38.470
Water Gun!

00:14:51.400 --> 00:14:52.490
It hit!

00:14:53.490 --> 00:14:57.000
Oh! You were trying
to harden the sand with water?

00:14:57.370 --> 00:14:58.870
Exactly!

00:14:58.870 --> 00:15:00.500
Messon! Water Gun!

00:15:00.500 --> 00:15:02.080
Riolu! Vacuum Wave!

00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:46.750
That’s Dragon Dive.

00:15:54.740 --> 00:15:56.330
M-M-M-M—

00:15:56.330 --> 00:15:57.600
Messon, get back! Fast!

00:15:59.600 --> 00:16:00.600
Vacuum Wave!

00:16:03.630 --> 00:16:05.060
We can’t hit!

00:16:05.810 --> 00:16:07.770
Should I change my strategy?

00:16:07.770 --> 00:16:11.610
No, fighting up close
is too dangerous...

00:16:11.610 --> 00:16:13.910
But... But...!

00:16:16.000 --> 00:16:18.490
What am I gonna do?!

00:16:19.580 --> 00:16:21.460
Here it comes, Satoshi!

00:16:32.790 --> 00:16:34.650
Are you okay, Satoshi?!

00:16:43.110 --> 00:16:45.210
Can you go on, Rabbifoot?

00:16:50.620 --> 00:16:51.650
Double Kick!

00:17:04.960 --> 00:17:07.420
Rabbifoot! Listen for the sound!

00:17:14.490 --> 00:17:17.050
You dodged it?!
Rabbifoot, that’s amazing!

00:17:21.930 --> 00:17:23.430
Now! Ember!

00:17:31.280 --> 00:17:32.780
Another Ember!

00:17:39.580 --> 00:17:42.850
It’s no use...
Flygon is so much faster!

00:17:51.250 --> 00:17:52.150
It’s Draco Meteor!

00:17:52.150 --> 00:17:52.880
Dodge it!

00:18:04.140 --> 00:18:07.140
Don’t get too far away!
Dodge while moving in!

00:18:08.330 --> 00:18:11.020
Why?! That’s crazy!

00:18:11.020 --> 00:18:13.150
Fighting from a distance is much...

00:18:18.530 --> 00:18:21.630
What? What is Go thinking?

00:18:23.620 --> 00:18:27.010
Now! Use the Draco Meteors
as footing and close in!

00:18:27.010 --> 00:18:27.500
What?!

00:18:39.010 --> 00:18:40.770
Kick the meteor and use Ember!

00:18:48.840 --> 00:18:53.000
All right!
Go, Monster Ball!

00:19:05.810 --> 00:19:09.160
Flygon’s data will be
added to the Index!

00:19:11.520 --> 00:19:13.430
We did it!

00:19:13.430 --> 00:19:18.340
Amazing, Rabbifoot!
Absolutely amazing!

00:19:18.340 --> 00:19:21.680
Jumping on top of the meteors
and using them for Ember...

00:19:22.950 --> 00:19:25.730
That’s such a crazy tactic!

00:19:25.730 --> 00:19:29.430
What are you on about?
You’re the one who taught it to me.

00:19:30.710 --> 00:19:35.610
No matter how crazy you have to be,
never stop striving for victory.

00:19:36.260 --> 00:19:39.650
I figured this was the kind of thing
<i>you’d</i> normally do.

00:19:41.680 --> 00:19:46.200
Besides, I really wanted
to settle the match with Ember.

00:19:47.040 --> 00:19:51.080
Because that’s the move Rabbifoot
and I made together!

00:19:54.320 --> 00:19:57.240
We couldn’t just give up
and stay the losers, yeah?

00:19:59.530 --> 00:20:01.430
I’m sure Rabbifoot felt the same.

00:20:06.870 --> 00:20:09.390
I see.

00:20:10.840 --> 00:20:16.310
Ever since I lost to Otosupus,
I’ve been dead-set on fighting at a distance...

00:20:17.440 --> 00:20:21.030
Maybe back then, Riolu...

00:20:21.900 --> 00:20:24.110
Yeah...

00:20:24.110 --> 00:20:28.120
We’ve been training with
melee Fighting moves all along.

00:20:32.980 --> 00:20:34.970
If we use Ember and still lose,

00:20:34.970 --> 00:20:38.420
we’ll just have to think of a way to use Ember
that’ll let us win next time!

00:20:38.420 --> 00:20:44.510
The same move’s power can double, even triple
depending on the trainer's creativity!

00:20:44.510 --> 00:20:48.180
Battling sure is complex,
isn’t it, Satoshi?

00:20:59.250 --> 00:21:04.830
H-Hey, Satoshi?! Uh-oh...
Did the shock from all his losses get to him?!

00:21:04.830 --> 00:21:07.070
I sure am stupid.

00:21:08.570 --> 00:21:11.790
I’ll have to start over.

00:21:13.200 --> 00:21:15.460
Pikachu. Riolu.

00:21:16.150 --> 00:21:19.360
I’ll try hard to face Mr. Dande again.

00:21:19.360 --> 00:21:21.000
Will you help me?

00:21:26.100 --> 00:21:28.420
I see. Thank you.

00:21:29.100 --> 00:21:33.580
All right! I’ll keep it up
and catch more big shots!

00:21:35.190 --> 00:21:39.550
Go grew a little, and Satoshi
has reconsidered his approach a little.

00:21:39.550 --> 00:21:42.800
But they still have a long way to go
to reach their dreams!

00:21:49.990 --> 00:21:50.280
(Mew → Zamazenta Ver.)
Pokémon Shiritori

